    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The word Chalcolithic is derived from two words: - <em>Chalco </em>meaning copper - <em>Lithic </em>meaning stone",
      "id": "qwkyens"
    },
    {
      "id": "f5v6z6z",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "Features"
    },
    {
      "id": "3vm2frp",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Use of both stone and copper tools.",
        "Agriculture was well developed.",
        "Painted pottery was used."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Important SSC Point: Chalcolithic Age should not be confused with the Bronze Age. Bronze is an alloy of copper and tin, while Chalcolithic tools used only copper.",
      "id": "au564qy"
    },
    {
      "id": "4uplo5h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Comparative Overview (Very Important for Exams)"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Chalcolithic Age is characterized by the combined use of both stone and copper tools.",
        "Bronze is an alloy of copper and tin, whereas Chalcolithic tools relied solely on copper.",
        "Prehistoric evolutionary code H–M–F–C represents Hunting → Microliths → Farming → Copper.",
        "Agriculture and the first use of pottery began during the Neolithic Age.",
        "Key regional sites include Soan Valley (Paleolithic), Bagor (Mesolithic), and Mehrgarh (Neolithic)."
      ],
      "id": "z43lm9v"
    },
